        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 4: Cross-model summary of contamination findings. (a) Dataset-level ASW comparison between PBMC 3k (contaminated) and AIDA v2 (clean) for Geneformer V1 and scGPT-human. Note: this naive between-dataset comparison is confounded by labeling asymmetry (PBMC labels from k-means on 8 clusters versus AIDA labels from 30+ ontology terms); the matched-k analysis in Table 6 shows the apparent inflation collapses to ≤ 5% under matched labels, and the rigorous donor-controlled effect is reported in Section 5.4 and Fig. 3. Panel shown for completeness. (b) Within-cell-type tightness gap per pancreatic cell type without donor matching, for Geneformer V1 (6/7 cell types positive, mean +1.28%) and scGPT-human (7/7 positive, mean +0.75%). UCE-4L's larger magnitude is shown separately in Fig. 3. This analysis is informative but does not control for donor identity; the donor-matched analysis in Table 7 and Fig. 3 provides the statistically rigorous effect-size estimate. (c) Signal A audit: % of cells flagged at p < 0.05 for each benchmark, color-coded by contamination status (red: contaminated; green: clean).</div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
